# =============================================================================
# public/_headers — ONLY used by Netlify / Cloudflare Pages style static hosts.
# Vercel IGNORES this file: production headers live in vercel.json (the source of
# truth), and local dev headers in server.js. Keep all three in sync —
# test/headers-parity.test.mjs fails CI when HSTS / COOP / CORP / CSP / noindex drift.
#
# Written for Cloudflare Pages semantics: a later block uses "! Header" to detach
# the value set by the catch-all before replacing it. (Netlify would instead
# COMBINE duplicate headers — two CSPs are both enforced — so on Netlify move the
# per-page CSPs into netlify.toml instead of relying on this file.)
#
# NOTE: script-src is HASH-BASED — 'unsafe-inline' has been removed; each inline
# <script> is allowed by its sha256 (regenerate with `npm run gen:csp` after editing
# any inline script). style-src still allows 'unsafe-inline' (documented accepted
# risk for inline styles). Do not add hosts back to script-src.
# =============================================================================

